<title>SINGAPORE: Chemical Industries half year net slips.</title>
<headline>Chemical Industries half year net slips.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to September 30 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			1.35    vs    2.82</p>
<p>    Group share (cts)	     3.40    vs    7.10</p>
<p>    Turnover			 14.28    vs   13.99</p>
<p>    Other income/interest	 0.93    vs    1.39</p>
<p>    Interest expense		1.44    vs    1.26</p>
<p>    Depreciation,amortisation   0.55    vs    0.56</p>
<p>    Associates		     (0.04)   vs    0.92</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		  2.33    vs    3.02</p>
<p>    Tax				 0.89    vs    0.92</p>
<p>    Extraordinary		   0.90    vs    nil</p>
<p>    Minorities			0.32    vs    nil</p>
<p>Note - Chemical Industries (Far East) Ltd said its performance was affected by weak global prices and spot supply excesses. An extraordinary gain of S$580,000 was obtained from the sale of a foreign investment. The group expects to maintain its profitability in the current year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
